  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building Capacities of Frontline Officers to Tackle Trafficking in Persons and Related Cross-Border Crimes at Land and Sea Borders in Viet Nam - Phase II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Capacity building for frontline Border Guard officers at land and sea border areas has been identified as important particularly at the local level to enable frontline officers to handle high caseloads appropriately, especially in the face of relative &#x2018;new&#x2019; forms of Trafficking in Persons (TIP) crime[1] that have been on the rise in recent years. The project aims to strengthen the capacities of law enforcement authorities at land borders so that they can effectively identify and counteract TIP and the smuggling of migrants. The project builds on the established partnerships with the VBG, especially the Department of Drug Control and Crime Prevention (DDCCP) and the Department of Border Gates (DBG), whose technical capacities for trafficking investigation and victim identification, support, and protection will be supported with (i) the endorsed standard training curriculum and (ii) roll-out training in hotspot provinces across three regions of Viet Nam. The project will also contribute to enhancing the implementation of national and regional border management and anti-crime strategies including the National Plan of Action against Human Trafficking 2021-2025, the National Implementation Plan of the Global Compact for Safe, Orderly and Regular Migration (GCM), and the ASEAN Convention Against Trafficking in Persons.</narrative>
  </description>
